WEBVTT

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.670
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.960
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.520
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.770
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.370
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.680
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.960
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.090
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.960
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.940
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.710
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.140
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.650
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.880
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:14.080
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.680
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.920
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.300
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:38.500
It's true! A star fell down and then
there was a light in the desert.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:40.910
Right. And where did
you see this light?

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.870
The desert to the west.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.140
I saw the same flash
about 3 days ago, too.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.040
Thanks.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.020
Shiro, that intel was right!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.950
<i>Contact headquarters</i>
<i>and every team in the area.</i>

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.330
<i>Hey! Did you hear me?</i>

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.490
<i>Michel!</i>

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.150
Yes, sir! What is it?

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.860
<i>Contact headquarters!</i>

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.860
<i>Aye, sir. Go ahead.</i>

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.390
<i>The 08th Team has</i>
<i>discovered evidence...</i>

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.960
<i>...of the location of the</i>
<i>Zeon weapons testing ground.</i>

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.240
<i>We're moving in to confirm.</i>

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.500
<i>Roger.</i>

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.450
There it goes again...
This is Shiro.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.460
<i>My left foot's acting up</i>
<i>again. Go on ahead of me.</i>

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.930
<i>Will you be okay by yourself?</i>

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.630
<i>Michel and I will manage somehow.</i>

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.470
<i>Roger.</i>

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.300
<i>I don't read any radiation.</i>

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.370
<i>Roger.</i>

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:21.100
One, two... Pull!

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.080
How's it look?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.860
Right, right.
I'm getting to it.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.870
Glass?! A beam weapon's
melted this to glass.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:01.080
Commander! The pack-in's
screwed up...

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.520
...and the filter's
clogged with sand!

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.280
Could I have an
M-18 filter, please?

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.480
Hold on a second!

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.330
<i>The angle of fire indicates</i>
<i>it came from low altitude.</i>

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.800
This has to be
the testing ground.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.690
<i>Aye, sir.</i>

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.730
See? Told you it was here.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:19.690
Looks that way...

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.910
You called this one right, Kiki.
I appreciate this.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.470
Of course you appreciate it!

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.740
You'd better stay here.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.840
We'll handle it from here.
Be careful on your way home.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.180
You heard the man...

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.340
...little lady.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.320
Who said I was going home?!

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.380
Michel, get in
the cockpit, okay?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.480
Aye, sir.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.990
<i>A beam weapon... A high-energy</i>
<i>beam weapon, at that.</i>

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:53.500
It has to be that monster!

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:02.240
Michel, move the leg a little.
Just a little!

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.710
A- Aye, sir!

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.680
Michel! Stop it!

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.340
Shiro!

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.260
Hurry up!

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.360
What are you doing?!

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.940
Are you trying
to kill Shiro?!

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:37.040
I- I was just... Thank you.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.580
Commander! Are you all right?!

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.880
I'm still alive. Somehow.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.350
Okay?! Don't fall
asleep like that!

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.720
<i>Oh, man... B.B....</i>

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.010
Michel! Erase my footprints.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.880
<i>I'm doing it right now.</i>

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.980
<i>Michel, wipe out my</i>
<i>footprints, too, okay?</i>

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.620
Roger.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.780
<i>Michel, do a point check</i>
<i>on the balloons, too.</i>

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.380
Michel, do you understand?

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.260
Switch to wired systems.
Cut out the wireless.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:30.230
Roger! "Michel! Michel!"

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.560
I'm only one person!

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:36.370
I can't do everything
at once! Jeez!

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.580
<i>Get it together, Michel!</i>
<i>You're on a mission!</i>

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.810
<i>And don't make excuses</i>
<i>because Eledore's not here!</i>

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.510
I'm not doing that... yet...

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.180
I haven't even finished getting
ready to set everything up.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.350
<i>Michel?</i>

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.290
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.190
You guys can head back.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.200
Well... But...

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:06.170
Are you saying we should
just leave you here?

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.300
The Feds are only doing
this because of my info.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.310
I have to see this
through to the end.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.670
Gee, I wonder why you wanna help
their commander out so much.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:26.920
See you.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.650
Just shut up! You jerks!

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.100
Enemy unit that
has entered the gully...

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.160
...is headed for point Delta
in the testing site.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:50.080
<i>Initiate Minovsky particle</i>
<i>broadcast. All set, Michel?</i>

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.710
Aye, sir.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:54.010
<i>Passing point Alpha!</i>

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.450
<i>Karen! Raise the balloons!</i>

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:02.360
<i>Balloons raised!</i>
<i>Retreat path is closed!</i>

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:05.290
Simulation confirmed.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.560
<i>Sanders, you ready</i>
<i>to pick it off?</i>

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.560
Locked on.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.630
Simulation confirmed!
Point Bravo!

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.630
Release the net and
create a blind alley!

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:21.940
<i>Net released!</i>

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:23.030
<i>Confirmed!</i>

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.070
Passing point Charlie!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.610
All right!
Now concentrate all fire...

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:31.240
<i>...on the area right in</i>
<i>front of point Delta!</i>

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.550
<i>This time, we'll get you!</i>

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.000
What happened?!

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.760
<i>Would you wake the hell UP?!</i>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:53.740
B- But, I...

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:56.610
<i>You have to stay doubly alert</i>
<i>now that Eledore isn't there!</i>

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.540
That's not what!

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.310
No, I- I'm sorry.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:14.690
Hey, Commander! I brought
some water and food for you.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.460
You're still here?

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.140
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.470
And after I bring
all this out to you.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:33.910
If this turns into a battle zone,
I can't guarantee your safety.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.760
Did you hear me?

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:48.120
I can fix that rip
in your clothes.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.160
Never mind it.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.830
<i>Take it off and I'll mend it.</i>

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.830
<i>I said never mind!</i>

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.340
<i>What are you</i>
<i>being so shy about?</i>

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.930
<i>Hey! Cut it out!</i>

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:02.200
<i>Why are you giving</i>
<i>me such a hard time?</i>

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.250
<i>Come on! Hurry up</i>
<i>and take it off!</i>

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:06.670
<i>A- All right, just this once.</i>

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:10.520
What are they doing?

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.150
Hey, Karen? Do you read me?

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.130
Hm? What's wrong?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.930
No... Never mind.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.700
What are you doing?

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:33.230
Water's precious.
In case we need it.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.690
It hasn't even
been a half hour?

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.560
<i>Shiro! Shiro!</i>

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.970
Is something wrong?!

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:02.700
Can I come over there?
l fixed your shirt.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.310
<i>What do I need a
shirt for in this heat?!</i>

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.430
It'll get cold at night.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.240
Michel! Any word from
the other units?

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.150
Um... Nothing at all, sir.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.980
<i>Don't let her tie up</i>
<i>our comm system then!</i>

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.580
Just because he's a commander...

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.790
...does that mean he has
to be such a hard-ass?

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:32.730
Hey, Kiki... You've got a crush
on the commander, don't you?

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.940
Is this a letter
from your girlfriend?

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.670
Stop that! Give it back!

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.870
"Michel, thank you for
all the letters"!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:47.440
I said cut it out!

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.280
"The letters you send me..."

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:53.510
"...are the one comfort
I have as I wait for you!"

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:56.720
Oh, I can't STAND it!

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.820
"But, but... I'm always afraid."

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:03.990
"Because I'm always wondering if
this will be your last letter."

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.660
"I feel as though the war..."

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.500
"...is taking you further
and further away from me."

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:17.410
"And I'm afraid that one day
the letters will stop coming."

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:20.910
"I don't think I can
take this anymore."

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:23.110
"With all that,
it might be easier for me...

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:25.980
"...to just forget about you..."

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:31.080
I can't read anymore.
I'm sorry.

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:33.150
It's all right.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.900
I'm going to
make it back alive.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:41.300
My feelings... aren't lessened
by our distance apart.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:50.270
No matter what I say or what I write,
why doesn't she understand that?

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:52.310
I understand
how she feels, too.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.080
You do?

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.980
The feelings you have...

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.280
All you can do is
keep throwing them at her.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:03.190
That's all that I know.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:07.150
Maybe you're right.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.930
The thing is...

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.190
I'm too far away to hit
her with those feelings.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:17.030
Sometimes you can be too far away
even when you're right next to them...

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:26.310
Maybe it'll come tomorrow...
Maybe it'll come.

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:47.360
Beans never seem to go
down smoothly for me.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.100
Hey, I'll get those myself.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:52.830
I cooked that well
for you, didn't I?

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.570
It tasted good, but...

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.870
But how long are you...

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.040
Commander!

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:00.510
How long? Until it comes?

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:02.820
Dunno.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:05.120
It's been 5 days now.

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.980
I thought you said this
would take 3 days at most.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:15.020
Yeah, I'd like to take a nice
long shower and drink a cold beer.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.360
This heat's driving me nuts.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.970
I... I!

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:28.210
I can't take this anymore!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:35.610
As long as I'm stuck out here,
I can't get a letter mailed!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.910
And B.B.'s waiting for me!
Dammit! Dammit!

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.190
Michel...

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:45.060
We all have our
own private problems.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.290
What do you mean?

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:51.400
Say, I can carry a
letter back for you.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:56.090
A letter?

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:58.260
I'll go for you.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.600
I just have to get it to
your headquarters, right?

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:04.600
My people have too
much free time anyway.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.070
Kiki...

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.810
Whoa! Just a minute!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.210
What's wrong?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.850
Would you two stop
treating this like a picnic?!

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:14.120
We don't do things
because we feel like it.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:15.780
We do what
we're ordered to do.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:18.850
WE do things that
WE decide to do!

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.230
I don't remember
making you my leader!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.860
Look, I appreciate
all your help...

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.090
...but could you stop
butting into our business?!

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:30.630
Stop butting into
your business, huh?!

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:35.010
Did you get an order
saying he CAN'T send a letter?!

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.180
Let go! How long are
you gonna hang onto me?!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.310
What's she so hysterical about?

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:47.850
The one who's
hysterical... is you, Shiro!

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.260
You idiot.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:52.720
Kiki?!

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.890
Commander!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.590
Why couldn't you
be nicer to her?!

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.130
You don't understand
girls' feelings at all!

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.310
Haven't you ever
been in love?!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:14.240
Isn't that why you take such
good care of that girl's watch?!

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.480
Michel!

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.650
Is unrequited love the
only kind you know about?!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:26.750
I don't think that's
any of your business!

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.330
You think you can understand
everyone's feelings?!

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:34.130
Better that than someone who
doesn't TRY understand them!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.530
Michel!

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.870
When you understand them...

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.530
...it's even harder for you to tell
those feelings to the other person!

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:44.070
I think you're a disgrace!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.980
Enough! You've said enough.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:02.220
Yeah. That may be the
best way. I'll head back.

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:04.700
Michel, you drive
the mobile suit.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:07.020
Switch with me.

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:08.400
I couldn't do that.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:11.130
If we leave you in charge of
the truck in your condition...

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.110
...the 08th Team will end up dead!

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.220
What's wrong with me?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:37.290
It's like even I don't
know how I really feel.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:41.670
It's cold.
And it'll wake you up.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.460
I thought water was precious.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.940
Just have some. You need it.

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:49.100
Thank you. By the way...

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:51.370
Talking isn't my strong point.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.120
Why do things
have to be this way?

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:06.030
Aina Sahalin...
Does she have a boyfriend?

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:10.090
I shouldn't be
surprised if she does.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.460
Dammit, it's just
like Michel said.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.960
<i>Commander.</i>
<i>This song on the radio...</i>

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.060
<i>It's Eledore's song.</i>

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.840
...shikanai yone
...can't help, right?

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:21.900
<i>Eledore's?</i>

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:28.950
Kasa ne au samishisa wa,
This overlapping loneliness,

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:35.680
nukumori o oshiete kureta
teach me about it warmly...

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:35.880
Nice song.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.190
Dakiaeba namida sae,
Let's embrace each other even in tears,

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.630
Yeah.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:39.860
Dakiaeba namida sae,
Let's embrace each other even in tears,

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.940
What was wrong
with me, anyway?

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:43.700
wake mo naku... miyou yo
unconditionally... why don't we?

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:46.460
<i>And that song was a request</i>
<i>from someone in a field hospital.</i>

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:46.540
wake mo naku... miyou yo
unconditionally... why don't we?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.940
<i>From Petty Officer Eledore Massis,</i>
<i>honorably wounded in action.</i>

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.600
<i>Okay, next up on our play list...</i>

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:55.340
What? The guy requested
his own song?!

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:57.970
That idiot.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.520
That's SO like Eledore!

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:08.120
That's one guy who's totally
honest with himself!

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.770
Initiating Minovsky
particle broadcast!

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.740
Everyone! Get ready!

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:27.700
<i>Karen!</i>

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:29.610
<i>Point Charlie,</i>
<i>sighted and locked!</i>

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:31.870
Michel! Aim well!

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:32.970
<i>Aye, sir.</i>

00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:35.020
Raise output on beam weaponry.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:36.450
<i>Commander.</i>

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.380
What is it?

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:42.510
I'm sorry. About yesterday.
I shouldn't have said that.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:44.590
No big deal.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.220
<i>Aye, sir!</i>

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:46.420
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:51.260
I'm not going to die!
B.B., believe in me and wait!

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:55.130
All I can do... is keep
throwing my feelings at you!

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.230
<i>Passing point Alpha!</i>
<i>I only see the monster.</i>

00:19:58.570 --> 00:19:59.940
<i>Raise the balloons!</i>

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.220
Locked on!

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:32.300
Mobile suits with beam weaponry!
Escort units, do you read me?!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.780
<i>Michel!</i>

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.900
<i>Commander, two fighters,</i>
<i>coming in high!</i>

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:12.300
Locked on!

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:28.090
MICHEL!!!

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:03.660
<i>God dammit! Die already!</i>

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:09.060
Let go of me!
Do you want to get killed?!

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:13.110
That voice... It can't be!

00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:23.310
<i>Dammit! Dammit!</i>

00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:29.560
<i>COMMANDER!</i>

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:31.890
God dammit! I lost it!

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:36.160
It can't be... Shiro...
Where did he go?!

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.060
SHIRO!!!

00:22:51.400 --> 00:22:54.140
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:57.830
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:57.910 --> 00:23:01.970
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:02.050 --> 00:23:05.740
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.910
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:12.920
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:17.050
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:20.190
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:23.330
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:28.200
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:34.070
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:38.410
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:43.310
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:47.080
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:54.220
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:58.330
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:02.400
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:02.470 --> 00:24:06.140
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:12.830
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:20.310
I can't believe Aina is the
pilot of that new Zeon weapon!

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:22.070
In a life or death
situation like that...

00:24:22.150 --> 00:24:23.980
...I nearly ended
up killing her!

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:27.020
But as soon as we confirm
that each other is safe...

00:24:27.080 --> 00:24:29.050
...we find ourselves racing
towards a huge mountain range!

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:31.680
We have to find some
way to save ourselves.

00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:35.420
Aina! Live or die,
we're doing it together!

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:40.990
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:41.070 --> 00:24:42.590
"Reunion."
